b2g_konzessiv	0	🔀	Concede, then disagree	You can agree with part of what someone says, then make your own point.	Obwohl es spät ist, bleibe ich.	[{"key": "learn", "label": "Learn", "steps": [{"t": "story", "lines": ["At B2 you are rarely asked to just agree or just disagree.", "You are asked to do both: give the other side something, then make your point.", "That move runs on four words."]}, {"t": "teach", "w": 0}, {"q": "Which one is <b>obwohl</b>?", "t": "pick", "from": [0, 1]}, {"t": "teach", "w": 1}, {"q": "Which one is <b>trotzdem</b>?", "t": "pick", "from": [1, 0]}, {"t": "hack", "body": "Obwohl es spät <b>ist</b>, bleibe ich. — But trotzdem does not: Es ist spät. Trotzdem bleibe ich.", "title": "obwohl throws the verb to the end."}, {"t": "teach", "w": 2}, {"t": "teach", "w": 3}, {"t": "match", "ws": [0, 1, 2, 3]}, {"t": "build", "de": ["Obwohl", "es", "spät", "ist", "bleibe", "ich"], "en": "Although it is late, I am staying.", "hard": true, "extra": ["trotzdem"]}, {"t": "spotmistake", "tokens": ["Ich", "bin", "müde,", "obwohl", "arbeite", "ich", "weiter"], "context": "A colleague writes in the handover:", "shouldBe": "trotzdem", "wrongIdx": 3}, {"t": "speak", "de": "Obwohl es spät ist, bleibe ich.", "en": "Although it is late, I am staying."}], "teaches": [["obwohl", "although", "🔀"], ["trotzdem", "all the same", "🔀"], ["dennoch", "even so", "🔀"], ["zwar", "admittedly", "🔀"]]}, {"key": "use", "label": "Use it", "steps": [{"t": "story", "lines": ["Now the version you will actually write at work."]}, {"t": "teach", "w": 0}, {"t": "teach", "w": 1}, {"t": "teach", "w": 2}, {"t": "hack", "body": "Say the concession with <b>zwar</b>, then turn it with <b>aber</b>: Der Plan steht <b>zwar</b> fest, <b>aber</b> wir brauchen eine Ausnahme.", "title": "zwar … aber is one move, not two words."}, {"t": "teach", "w": 3}, {"t": "translate", "de": "Der Dienstplan steht fest. Trotzdem brauchen wir eine Ausnahme.", "en": ["The", "shift", "schedule", "is", "fixed", "All", "the", "same", "we", "need", "an", "exception"], "extra": ["although"]}, {"t": "build", "de": ["Der", "Plan", "steht", "zwar", "fest", "aber", "wir", "brauchen", "eine", "Ausnahme"], "en": "Admittedly the plan is fixed, but we need an exception.", "hard": true}, {"t": "chat", "who": "Stationsleitung", "goal": "Concede that the schedule is fixed — then ask for the exception anyway.", "turns": [{"en": "{name}, the shift schedule has been fixed since Monday.", "opts": [{"de": "Der Plan steht zwar fest, aber ich brauche eine Ausnahme.", "en": "Admittedly the plan is fixed, but I need an exception.", "ok": true}, {"de": "Ja, der Plan steht fest.", "en": "Yes, the plan is fixed."}], "them": "{name}, der Dienstplan steht seit Montag fest."}, {"en": "And why should I do that?", "opts": [{"de": "Obwohl es kurzfristig ist, finde ich einen Tausch.", "en": "Although it is short notice, I will find a swap.", "ok": true}, {"de": "Trotzdem ich einen Tausch finde.", "en": "(not German)"}], "them": "Und warum sollte ich das machen?"}], "avatar": "🗓️"}, {"t": "speakcards", "cards": [{"de": "Obwohl es spät ist, bleibe ich.", "en": "Although it is late, I am staying."}, {"de": "Der Plan steht zwar fest, aber wir brauchen eine Ausnahme.", "en": "Admittedly the plan is fixed, but we need an exception."}, {"de": "Es ist kurzfristig. Trotzdem finde ich einen Tausch.", "en": "It is short notice. All the same, I will find a swap."}]}], "teaches": [["allerdings", "however", "🔀"], ["der Dienstplan", "the shift schedule", "🗓️"], ["die Ausnahme", "the exception", "🔓"], ["zwar … aber", "admittedly … but", "🔀"]]}]	b2	retired	a1_methodology_conflict	2026-09-07 18:37:20.348673+05:30
b2g_konjunktiv2	1	🎚️	Suggest without demanding	You can propose something so it lands as a suggestion, not an order.	Man könnte die Übergabe früher machen.	[{"key": "learn", "label": "Learn", "steps": [{"t": "story", "lines": ["„Wir machen die Übergabe früher.“ — that is a decision you just announced.", "One vowel turns it into a suggestion someone can say yes to."]}, {"t": "teach", "w": 0}, {"q": "Which one is <b>könnte</b>?", "t": "pick", "from": [0, 1]}, {"t": "teach", "w": 2}, {"q": "Which one is <b>wäre</b>?", "t": "pick", "from": [2, 3]}, {"t": "hack", "body": "kann → <b>könnte</b>, muss → <b>müsste</b>, war → <b>wäre</b>, hatte → <b>hätte</b>. Same verb, softer claim.", "title": "The umlaut is the whole trick."}, {"t": "teach", "w": 1}, {"t": "teach", "w": 3}, {"t": "match", "ws": [0, 1, 2, 3]}, {"t": "build", "de": ["Das", "wäre", "eine", "gute", "Lösung"], "en": "That would be a good solution.", "hard": true, "extra": ["ist"]}, {"t": "spotmistake", "tokens": ["Wir", "machen", "die", "Übergabe", "früher"], "context": "In a written proposal to the ward manager:", "shouldBe": "könnten", "wrongIdx": 1}, {"t": "speak", "de": "Das wäre eine gute Lösung.", "en": "That would be a good solution."}], "teaches": [["könnte", "could", "🎚️"], ["müsste", "would have to", "🎚️"], ["wäre", "would be", "🎚️"], ["hätte", "would have", "🎚️"]]}, {"key": "use", "label": "Use it", "steps": [{"t": "story", "lines": ["Now put it where it earns its keep: a proposal someone can accept."]}, {"t": "teach", "w": 0}, {"t": "teach", "w": 1}, {"t": "teach", "w": 2}, {"t": "teach", "w": 3}, {"t": "hack", "body": "<b>Man könnte …</b> (one could) and <b>Es wäre sinnvoll, wenn …</b> (it would make sense if). Both leave the other person room to agree.", "title": "Two openers that carry a whole proposal."}, {"t": "build", "de": ["Man", "könnte", "die", "Übergabe", "früher", "machen"], "en": "One could do the handover earlier.", "hard": true, "extra": ["muss"]}, {"t": "translate", "de": "Es wäre sinnvoll, wenn wir früher anfangen.", "en": ["It", "would", "be", "sensible", "if", "we", "start", "earlier"], "extra": ["is"]}, {"t": "chat", "who": "Stationsleitung", "goal": "Make the proposal — as a proposal, not an announcement.", "turns": [{"en": "You wanted to propose something, {name}?", "opts": [{"de": "Man könnte die Übergabe früher machen.", "en": "One could do the handover earlier.", "ok": true}, {"de": "Wir machen die Übergabe früher.", "en": "We are doing the handover earlier."}], "them": "Sie wollten etwas vorschlagen, {name}?"}, {"en": "Hm. And what does that achieve?", "opts": [{"de": "Es wäre sinnvoll, wenn wir mehr Zeit hätten.", "en": "It would be sensible if we had more time.", "ok": true}, {"de": "Es ist sinnvoll, weil wir mehr Zeit haben.", "en": "It is sensible because we have more time."}], "them": "Hm. Und was bringt das?"}], "avatar": "💡"}, {"t": "speakcards", "cards": [{"de": "Man könnte die Übergabe früher machen.", "en": "One could do the handover earlier."}, {"de": "Das wäre eine gute Lösung.", "en": "That would be a good solution."}, {"de": "Es wäre sinnvoll, wenn wir mehr Zeit hätten.", "en": "It would be sensible if we had more time."}]}], "teaches": [["die Übergabe", "the handover", "🔁"], ["der Vorschlag", "the proposal", "💡"], ["vorschlagen", "to propose", "💡"], ["sinnvoll", "sensible", "✅"]]}]	b2	retired	a1_methodology_conflict	2026-09-07 18:37:20.348673+05:30
b2g_genitiv	2	📐	wegen, trotz + Genitiv	You can give a reason in writing without the mistake examiners mark every time.	wegen des Notfalls — not wegen dem Notfall.	[{"key": "learn", "label": "Learn", "steps": [{"t": "story", "lines": ["Spoken German lets „wegen dem“ slide. Written German does not.", "It is one of the few errors an examiner can circle without thinking."]}, {"t": "teach", "w": 0}, {"t": "teach", "w": 1}, {"t": "hack", "body": "Masculine and neuter take <b>des</b> …<b>s</b>: wegen <b>des</b> Notfall<b>s</b>. Feminine takes <b>der</b>, with no ending: wegen <b>der</b> Verspätung.", "title": "wegen and trotz both take the Genitiv."}, {"t": "teach", "w": 2}, {"t": "teach", "w": 3}, {"q": "Which one goes with a feminine noun — <b>der</b> or <b>des</b>?", "t": "pick", "from": [3, 2]}, {"t": "build", "de": ["wegen", "des", "Notfalls"], "en": "because of the emergency", "hard": true, "extra": ["dem"]}, {"t": "spotmistake", "tokens": ["Wegen", "dem", "Notfall", "komme", "ich", "später"], "context": "In a written sick note:", "shouldBe": "des", "wrongIdx": 1}, {"t": "spotmistake", "tokens": ["Trotz", "der", "Verspätung", "schaffe", "ich", "die", "Übergabe"], "context": "In the same note, one line down:", "shouldBe": "der", "wrongIdx": 1}, {"t": "speak", "de": "Wegen des Notfalls komme ich später.", "en": "Because of the emergency I will be later."}], "teaches": [["wegen", "because of", "📐"], ["trotz", "despite", "📐"], ["des", "of the (m/n)", "📐"], ["der", "of the (f)", "📐"]]}, {"key": "use", "label": "Use it", "steps": [{"t": "story", "lines": ["Same rule, three more prepositions that follow it."]}, {"t": "teach", "w": 0}, {"t": "teach", "w": 1}, {"t": "teach", "w": 2}, {"t": "teach", "w": 3}, {"t": "hack", "body": "<b>wegen · trotz · aufgrund · innerhalb · außerhalb · angesichts</b> — all Genitiv. Learn them as one group and you never have to decide again.", "title": "The same list, every time."}, {"t": "match", "ws": [0, 1, 2, 3]}, {"t": "build", "de": ["Trotz", "der", "Verspätung", "schaffe", "ich", "die", "Übergabe"], "en": "Despite the delay I will make the handover.", "hard": true, "extra": ["dem"]}, {"t": "translate", "de": "Aufgrund des Notfalls war ich später.", "en": ["On", "account", "of", "the", "emergency", "I", "was", "later"], "extra": ["despite"]}, {"t": "spotmistake", "tokens": ["Innerhalb", "einem", "Monat", "bin", "ich", "wieder", "da"], "context": "In an email to the ward:", "shouldBe": "eines", "wrongIdx": 1}, {"t": "speakcards", "cards": [{"de": "Wegen des Notfalls komme ich später.", "en": "Because of the emergency I will be later."}, {"de": "Trotz der Verspätung schaffe ich die Übergabe.", "en": "Despite the delay I will make the handover."}, {"de": "Aufgrund des Notfalls war ich später.", "en": "On account of the emergency I was later."}]}], "teaches": [["der Notfall", "the emergency", "🚨"], ["die Verspätung", "the delay", "⏰"], ["aufgrund", "on account of", "📐"], ["innerhalb", "within", "📐"]]}]	b2	retired	a1_methodology_conflict	2026-09-07 18:37:20.348673+05:30
b2v_nvv	3	🔗	Noun-verb pairs that read as B2	You can use the fixed phrases examiners look for instead of the simple verb.	Wir müssen das in Betracht ziehen.	[{"key": "learn", "label": "Learn", "steps": [{"t": "story", "lines": ["German has a fixed pair for things you would say with one plain verb.", "„Wir denken darüber nach“ is fine. „Wir ziehen es in Betracht“ is B2.", "The verb is the part that is fixed — get that wrong and the phrase is gone."]}, {"t": "teach", "w": 0}, {"t": "teach", "w": 1}, {"t": "teach", "w": 2}, {"t": "hack", "body": "<b>unter Druck stehen</b> — never „unter Druck haben“. The noun is the easy half; examiners mark the verb.", "title": "The verb is not negotiable."}, {"t": "match", "ws": [0, 1, 2]}, {"t": "build", "de": ["Wir", "müssen", "das", "in", "Betracht", "ziehen"], "en": "We have to take that into consideration.", "hard": true, "extra": ["nehmen"]}, {"t": "spotmistake", "tokens": ["Das", "Team", "hat", "seit", "Wochen", "unter", "Druck"], "context": "In a written report:", "shouldBe": "steht", "wrongIdx": 2}, {"t": "speak", "de": "Wir müssen das in Betracht ziehen.", "en": "We have to take that into consideration."}], "teaches": [["in Betracht ziehen", "to take into consideration", "🔗"], ["zur Verfügung stehen", "to be available", "🔗"], ["unter Druck stehen", "to be under pressure", "🔗"]]}, {"key": "use", "label": "Use it", "steps": [{"t": "story", "lines": ["Three more. These three are what turn a description into an argument."]}, {"t": "teach", "w": 0}, {"t": "teach", "w": 1}, {"t": "teach", "w": 2}, {"t": "hack", "body": "<b>an seine Grenzen stoßen</b> names the problem. <b>unter die Lupe nehmen</b> asks for scrutiny. <b>einen Standpunkt vertreten</b> is you, taking a side.", "title": "Where each one belongs."}, {"t": "match", "ws": [0, 1, 2]}, {"t": "build", "de": ["Das", "System", "stößt", "an", "seine", "Grenzen"], "en": "The system is reaching its limits.", "hard": true, "extra": ["kommt"]}, {"t": "translate", "de": "Wir sollten den Dienstplan unter die Lupe nehmen.", "en": ["We", "should", "examine", "the", "shift", "schedule", "closely"], "extra": ["ignore"]}, {"t": "chat", "who": "Kollegin", "goal": "Make the case using the pairs, not the plain verbs.", "turns": [{"en": "The ward has been understaffed for weeks.", "opts": [{"de": "Das Team stößt an seine Grenzen.", "en": "The team is reaching its limits.", "ok": true}, {"de": "Das Team ist müde.", "en": "The team is tired."}], "them": "Die Station ist seit Wochen unterbesetzt."}, {"en": "And what do you suggest?", "opts": [{"de": "Wir sollten den Dienstplan unter die Lupe nehmen.", "en": "We should examine the shift schedule closely.", "ok": true}, {"de": "Wir sollten den Dienstplan ansehen.", "en": "We should look at the shift schedule."}], "them": "Und was schlägst du vor?"}], "avatar": "🔗"}, {"t": "speakcards", "cards": [{"de": "Das Team stößt an seine Grenzen.", "en": "The team is reaching its limits."}, {"de": "Wir sollten den Dienstplan unter die Lupe nehmen.", "en": "We should examine the shift schedule closely."}, {"de": "Ich vertrete einen klaren Standpunkt.", "en": "I hold a clear position."}]}], "teaches": [["an seine Grenzen stoßen", "to reach one's limits", "🔗"], ["unter die Lupe nehmen", "to examine closely", "🔍"], ["einen Standpunkt vertreten", "to hold a position", "🔗"]]}]	b2	retired	a1_methodology_conflict	2026-09-07 18:37:20.348673+05:30
b2_register_aufklaerung	12	📐	Für den Arzt oder für den Patienten?	pitching information appropriately for colleagues versus patients	Register anpassen im Stationsalltag	[{"key": "main", "label": "Register anpassen", "steps": [{"t": "story", "lines": ["Frau Sommer (68 Jahre) hatte gestern eine Knie-OP. In der Nacht entwickelte sie einen akuten Harnverhalt — 650 ml Restharn im Ultraschall. Nach steriler Einmalkatheterisierung flossen 600 ml ab.", "Das Labor meldet außerdem: Kalium bei 3,1 mmol/l (leicht erniedrigt). Sie hat eine Kalium-Infusion angehängt bekommen.", "Dieselbe klinische Situation — zwei völlig verschiedene Adressaten. Sie schreiben jetzt beide Texte."]}, {"t": "notice", "body": "An den Arzt: kurz, dicht, Passiv, Fachwörter (Harnverhalt, Restharn, Hypokaliämie, Einmalkatheterisierung). An die Patientin: zugewandt, verständlich, Ursache und Beruhigung ohne Fachchinesisch.", "title": "Register macht den Unterschied"}, {"t": "produce", "mode": "write", "prompt": "Schreiben Sie eine kurze, präzise Übergabenotiz für die ärztliche Visite (mind. 35 Wörter). Nutzen Sie den fachsprachlichen Berichtsstil (Passiv, nominale Fügungen, Fachterminologie).", "guidance": ["Wesentliche Fakten: Harnverhalt, Restharnmenge, Katheterisierung, Kaliumwert, Infusion.", "Sachlicher, verdichteter Berichtsstil (z. B. ‚Bei Z. n. … wurde … durchgeführt‘).", "Keine Umgangssprache, keine weitschweifigen Schilderungen."], "minWords": 35, "taskType": "workplace", "afterHints": ["Postoperativ entwickelte die Patientin einen akuten Harnverhalt.", "Nach steriler Einmalkatheterisierung wurden 600 ml Urin entleert.", "Aufgrund einer leichten Hypokaliämie wurde eine Kaliumsubstitution veranlasst."], "capabilities": ["adapt_register", "structure"], "experienceId": "exp_register_arzt"}, {"t": "produce", "mode": "write", "prompt": "Erklären Sie Frau Sommer die Situation verständlich und einfühlsam am Krankenbett (mind. 40 Wörter). Erklären Sie, warum der Katheter nötig war und was die Infusion bewirkt — ohne Fachjargon.", "guidance": ["Erklären Sie die Narkose-Nachwirkung in einfachen Worten.", "Vermeiden Sie Fachbegriffe wie ‚Hypokaliämie‘ oder ‚Harnverhalt‘.", "Beruhigen Sie die Patientin und sagen Sie, wie es weitergeht."], "minWords": 40, "taskType": "patientenkommunikation", "afterHints": ["Nach der Narkose braucht die Blase manchmal etwas Zeit, um wieder richtig zu arbeiten.", "Wir haben mit einem kleinen Schlauch nachgeholfen, damit der Druck nachlässt.", "Über die Infusion bekommen Sie einen wichtigen Mineralstoff, der im Blut etwas zu niedrig war."], "capabilities": ["adapt_register", "justify"], "experienceId": "exp_register_patient"}], "teaches": []}]	b2	live	\N	\N
